Yes — now the root cause is clear from your log.

The test is not actually stuck in sendFlexRequest(). It is retrying because your test sends a request body with HttpMethod.GET.

Your log explicitly says:

Request must not have a body: GET /test-endpoint

Then your RetryConfig sees that failure as a non-WebClientResponseException, returns true, and WebClient retries it. That's why it looks like it's looping.

There is also a second issue:

when(perfTestDeterminer.usePerfTestUrl()).thenReturn(false);

in @BeforeEach is an unnecessary Mockito stub because many tests don't invoke perfTestDeterminer. Remove it from setup and stub it only in the tests that need it.

