The critical fixes are these

1. Removed this from setup()

when(perfTestDeterminer.usePerfTestUrl())
    .thenReturn(false);

That was causing:

Unnecessary stubbings detected
line 114

Now it is only stubbed in the three tests that actually call it.

2. Changed GET + body to POST

Your failing tests had:

HttpMethod.GET,
requestBody

That's invalid with MockWebServer.

They are now:

HttpMethod.POST,
requestBody

This is the main reason your test was repeatedly retrying.

3. No @SpringBootTest

The class remains a lightweight unit test:

@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)

so you shouldn't get the 14-second Spring Boot startup anymore.


---

About this warning

This:

Mockito is currently self-attaching to enable the inline-mock-maker

is not the reason your tests are failing.

It's a JDK 21/Mockito warning about future Mockito/JDK behavior. You can address it later in your Gradle configuration. Don't change your tests because of that warning.

One thing to check before running

Your production sendFlexRequest() should currently have the body handling you decided on:

.body(
    requestBody == null
        ? BodyInserters.empty()
        : BodyInserters.fromValue(requestBody))

If it still has:

.bodyValue(requestBody == null ? Mono.empty() : requestBody)

then don't test the null body path yet—the production implementation itself needs to be corrected first.

With the class above, there are no GET requests carrying a body and no global Mockito stubbing that gets unused, so the two problems shown in your latest output are removed.